319	**Correct:**
320	
321	```typescript
322	type Config = Record&lt;string, string&gt;;
323	
324	// Or better - use a specific union for keys:
325	type Config = Record&lt;&quot;host&quot; | &quot;port&quot; | &quot;env&quot;, string&gt;;
326	```
327	
328	**Why:** `Record&lt;K, V&gt;` is more readable and composable than index signatures. When possible, use a
329	union for keys to get exhaustive checking.
330	
331	### 13. Use using for Resource Management
332	
333	**Wrong (agents do this):**
334	
335	```typescript
336	const file = openFile(&quot;data.txt&quot;);
337	try {
338	  processFile(file);
339	} finally {
340	  file.close();
341	}
342	```
343	
344	**Correct:**
345	
346	```typescript
347	using file = openFile(&quot;data.txt&quot;);
348	processFile(file);
349	// file.close() called automatically via Symbol.dispose
350	```
351	
352	**Why:** The `using` keyword (TypeScript 5.2+) provides deterministic resource cleanup via the
353	Disposable protocol, similar to Python&#x27;s `with` or C#&#x27;s `using`.
354	
355	## Patterns
356	
357	- Enable `strict: true` and `noUncheckedIndexedAccess: true` in every project
358	- Use `satisfies` for type validation without widening
359	- Use discriminated unions with a `type` or `kind` field for state modeling
360	- Use `as const` for configuration objects and route maps
361	- Use branded types for domain-specific IDs
362	- Use `import type` for all type-only imports
363	- Use exhaustive `switch` with `never` default for union handling
364	
365	## Anti-Patterns
366	
367	- NEVER use `any` - use `unknown` and narrow with type guards
368	- NEVER use `as` for type assertions unless you genuinely know more than the compiler
369	- NEVER use optional fields to model mutually exclusive states - use discriminated unions
370	- NEVER use `// @ts-ignore` or `// @ts-expect-error` without a comment explaining why
371	- NEVER use `enum` - use `as const` objects or union types instead
372	- NEVER use `Function` type - use specific function signatures
373	- NEVER disable strict mode for convenience
